      "caveat": "The cut was chosen from these patients to separate their OS as much as possible, so the split is optimistic in-sample: its naive log-rank p (9.5e-15) ignores the search and overstates the evidence, and the cut needs validation in an independent cohort before it is used. Scanned: 73 candidate cuts — the distinct values of TMB_NONSYNONYMOUS leaving between 10% and 90% of patients at or below them (at most 100, evenly spaced) — by the maximally selected standardized log-rank statistic (Lausen & Schumacher; R maxstat). The corrected p is from 1000 permutations of the marker over the patients (seed 1): the share whose own best cut does as well. High is TMB_NONSYNONYMOUS > 14.42 (19.4% of patients). TMB_NONSYNONYMOUS is the patient's value, or for a sample attribute the value of the patient's first sample by sample id; 0 patients with a survival time and no numeric value are left out. The status '1:…' is an event, anything else censored; times from each study's own baseline. Per CANCER_TYPE: the largest 8 values with at least 100 patients each get their own scan and permutation test (same seed); 3 other values (133 patients) are not scanned. Each stratum's cut is as optimistic as the overall one. Computed from per-patient rows inside each patient-level study."
